WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:06.800
Master how to steer AI models with a complete, adult-level Prompt Engineering course. It is taught, tutored, drilled, and graded entirely by AI.

00:06.800 --> 00:11.400
The dashboard gives learners a clear view of assignments, practice problems, their current module, and recent activity.

00:11.400 --> 00:16.400
The curriculum covers four weeks and twenty-eight topics, from foundations and core techniques to advanced patterns, applications, and safety.

00:16.400 --> 00:21.400
Lessons are available in short, medium, and long versions. For example, a few-shot prompting lesson explains how examples guide a model toward the pattern you need.

00:21.400 --> 00:28.200
When learners have a question, the section-scoped tutor uses the passage they are reading. It can explain why a model adds conversational filler even when JSON was requested.

00:28.200 --> 00:33.700
Adaptive practice asks learners to explain their reasoning, gives feedback, and adjusts difficulty as they build a streak.

00:33.700 --> 00:40.400
Assignments are graded with written rationale. Learners can see their score, understand the concepts they demonstrated, and review an authorship check.

00:40.400 --> 00:44.900
Performance analytics show course progress, practice accuracy, attempts, streaks, and the topics that need more work.

00:44.900 --> 00:50.940
Prompt Engineering brings the curriculum, the tutor, the grader, and the integrity check together in one room.